    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, we're having some issues on the line here. The sublimation transfers on our polyester blends aren't coming out vibrant enough. The colors look faded or washed out after the heat press. Can you help me troubleshoot the temperature and pressure settings for this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Faded colors on polyester blends during sublimation transfers are often a sign of insufficient heat or pressure, which is what the proper settings are meant to achieve. Try increasing your heat press temperature by 10-20 degrees Fahrenheit, and ensure you are applying consistent, firm pressure across the entire transfer area. Also, check your curing time; sometimes a slightly longer press time can help the dyes properly bond to the synthetic fibers.",
